  "smell_rule_desc": "The pinyin style rendering policy must be owned by one location. The rule enumerates every production function that holds its own conditional pinyin-style decision (an if/switch over the exported style constants or the Args.Style field) and reports the smell when that decision authority is spread over several owner functions or files (>= 2 files or >= 3 owner functions), so that a conceptual change to a style (adding one, or moving one between families) requires coordinated edits across the conversion pipeline. Test files and style references used purely as data (for example lookup-table keys) are not owners. Implemented as a custom go/analysis analyzer (singlechecker driver, golang.org/x/tools v0.17.0) embedded in smell_check.sh.",
